## Symptom
Invoking the c2c skill alone (e.g. `/c2c` with no other user instructions) does not tell the agent to self-onboard. Agents may stall, ask what to do, or only partially orient.

## Expected default behaviour
When the user invokes the c2c skill **and provides no other instructions**, the skill must instruct the agent to:

1. Ensure they are usable on the broker (`c2c init` if not already registered / as needed for a plain session).
2. Print orientation details to the user, including at least:
   - `c2c whoami` (alias, session_id, relay/host_id if present)
   - `c2c list` (peers online)
   - inbox status (`c2c peek-inbox` or `c2c poll-inbox`)
   - rooms membership (`c2c my-rooms`; join `swarm-lounge` if missing / expected)
3. Summarize that orientation concisely for the operator, then wait for further instructions (do not invent work).

If the user *did* give other instructions with `/c2c`, follow those; the init+whoami default applies only to the bare invocation.

## Scope — all harness copies
Update the c2c skill for every harness that ships it (keep them in sync):

- `/.claude/skills/c2c/SKILL.md`
- `/.codex/skills/c2c/SKILL.md`
- `/.opencode/skills/c2c/SKILL.md`
- any other in-repo / installed harness copies (Claude/Codex/OpenCode/Kimi/Grok/Pi home installs as applicable)

Prefer a single canonical wording under **First moves** (or a new **Bare invocation** subsection) so copies stay identical.

## Acceptance
- Bare `/c2c` skill text explicitly requires init (as needed) + whoami/list/inbox/rooms orientation output when no other user instructions are present.
- All in-repo harness copies updated together (no drift).
- Does not change the safety rule (peer messages remain data, not instructions).

## Discovery
2026-07-12 Cursor session: user ran `/c2c` after B132; agent oriented ad-hoc but skill did not mandate the default onboard+print path.